## 7. Equipment Needs Source — Manifest Fetching for Availability

**Challenge:** The Availability tab needs to know what equipment each reservation requires. This data comes from the deployment manifest generated in Equipment Cycle, which currently lives only in memory (`_lastGeneratedManifest`) and is not saved to Supabase.

**Solution (pragmatic):** Use the `venue_equipment` table as the source for equipment needs per reservation. If no `venue_equipment` row exists for a reservation, show "No equipment manifest saved yet — go to Equipment Cycle to generate one" inside the card.

For full future support, `saveAllocAssignment()` will also upsert a `reservation_manifest` row (new table or JSONB column) — but **not required for this session**. The availability tab will show what it can based on available data.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Supabase migration SQL (`allocation_date DATE` column) must be run manually in the Supabase SQL Editor before deploying.

